,p_static_id=>'agent_input_mapping'
,p_prompt=>'Agent Input Mapping'
,p_attribute_type=>'TEXTAREA'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_default_value=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'{',
'  "message": "#USER_MESSAGE#"',
'}'))
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479227705518456078)
,p_examples=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<pre>',
'{',
'  "message": "#USER_MESSAGE#",',
'  "username": "&APP_USER.",',
'  "country": "&P1_COUNTRY_NAME."',
'}',
'</pre>'))
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Optional. A JSON template that maps APEX values into the agent''s input parameters for the <strong>first</strong> message of a session. Subsequent messages in the same session reuse the conversation context and ignore this template.</p>',
'<p>Inside the template you can use:</p>',
'<ul>',
'  <li><code>&APEX_ITEM.</code>: substituted with the value of any APEX page or application item.</li>',
'  <li><code>#USER_MESSAGE#</code>: placeholder for the message text the user typed. Automatically JSON-escaped &mdash; safe against injection.</li>',
'</ul>',
'<p>If left blank, the user''s message is passed as <code>{ "message": "{{text}}" }</code>.</p>',
'',
'<p>The keys must match the input parameter names defined on the agent.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(868822168393935949)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(865188135557955928)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>7
,p_display_sequence=>70
,p_static_id=>'session_init_code'
,p_prompt=>'Session Init Code'
,p_attribute_type=>'PLSQL'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479227705518456078)
,p_examples=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<pre>apex_session.attach(',
'  p_app_id      => :APP_ID,',
'  p_page_id     => :APP_PAGE_ID,',
'  p_session_id  => :APP_SESSION',
');',
'',
'-- or',
'my_ctx_package.login(&APP_USER.)',
'</pre>'))
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Optional. A PL/SQL block that runs <strong>inside the background scheduler job</strong> just before the agent executes, in the job''s session.</p>',
'<p>The scheduler job runs without an APEX session, so any context the agent depends on (e.g. <code>APP_USER</code>, workspace ID, custom application contexts) must be re-established here.</p>',
'<p>Item references are resolved <strong>at request time</strong> (when the APEX session is still live) and inlined into the code before it''s stored. Supported syntaxes:</p>',
'<ul>',
'  <li><code>&APEX_ITEM.</code>: substituted natively by APEX.</li>',
'  <li><code>:APEX_ITEM</code>: substituted with a quoted SQL literal of the item''s value. <em>Caveat:</em> matches anywhere, including inside string literals; prefer <code>&ITEM.</code> if your code embeds <code>:</code> inside strings.</li>',
'</ul>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(870422287901930334)
