wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(477697405829392536)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(865188135557955928)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>17
,p_display_sequence=>170
,p_static_id=>'collect_feedback'
,p_prompt=>'Collect Feedback'
,p_attribute_type=>'CHECKBOX'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_default_value=>'N'
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479228396992456087)
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Lets the user rate the conversation with a thumbs up or thumbs down. On a thumbs down they can also leave an optional comment.</p>',
'',
'<p>A small <strong>Was this helpful?</strong> row sits under the newest answer and is always visible, so nothing is blocked and nobody is prompted. Expect only a small share of users to answer &ndash; that is the intent.</p>',
'',
'<p>One rating is stored per conversation, in <code>UC_AI_AGENT_SESSIONS.FEEDBACK_RATING</code> (with <code>FEEDBACK_COMMENT</code> and <code>FEEDBACK_AT</code>), so you can report on it &mdash; for example to list the conversations people were unhapp'
||'y with. <code>UC_AI_AGENTS_API.LIST_SESSIONS</code> returns all three columns.</p>',
'',
'<p>The user can change or withdraw their rating at any time; withdrawing also clears the comment.</p>',
'',
'<p>Requires UC AI 26.3 or later. Default: <strong>No</strong>.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(477697929950395442)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(865188135557955928)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>18
,p_display_sequence=>180
,p_static_id=>'suggested_prompts'
,p_prompt=>'Suggested Prompts'
,p_attribute_type=>'TEXTAREA'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479228396992456087)
,p_examples=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<pre>What is Oracle APEX?',
'Write a SQL query example',
'How do I debug a slow page?</pre>'))
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Example questions offered as clickable chips while the conversation is still empty. Clicking one sends it immediately, so a first-time user has something to try instead of a blank box.</p>',
'',
'<p>Enter <strong>one prompt per line</strong>. Surrounding spaces are trimmed and blank lines are ignored; commas and quotes are safe. Leave the attribute empty to show no chips.</p>',
'',
'<p>The chips show only while the transcript is empty and vanish as soon as the first message is sent &mdash; they are a starting point, not a menu. <strong>New chat</strong> empties the conversation, so they come back for the next one.</p>',
'',
'<p>Keep them short enough to read at a glance; long lines are still sent in full but wrap awkwardly in a narrow region.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479219325836276697)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(865188135557955928)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>19
,p_display_sequence=>190
,p_static_id=>'agent_run_context'
,p_prompt=>'Agent Run Context'
,p_attribute_type=>'TEXTAREA'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479227950721456087)
,p_examples=>'<pre>{ "contract_id": "&P10_CONTRACT_ID.", "tenant_id": "&APP_USER." }</pre>'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>A JSON object of name/value pairs that <strong>bind the conversation to specific data</strong> &mdash; one contract, one case, one tenant. UC AI passes them to every tool of the run under the reserved key <code>_ctx</code>.</p>',
'',
'<p>This is the difference between a tool that reads the contract the run is about and a tool that reads the contract the <em>model asked for</em>. The AI can neither see these values nor choose them, so leave the scoped value out of the tool&rsquo;s '
||'parameter schema and read it from <code>_ctx</code> in the handler &mdash; then there is exactly one place the value can come from.</p>',
'',
'<p>Values also fill prompt-profile placeholders that the input parameters do not supply, and the UC AI Pro memory layer can scope a store by one of the keys.</p>',
'',
'<p>Use <code>&amp;APEX_ITEM.</code> for any page or application item. Values are substituted after the JSON is parsed, so a value containing a quote or a backslash is escaped rather than breaking the object.</p>',
'',
'<p><code>#USER_MESSAGE#</code> is <strong>not</strong> supported here (it is removed if present) &mdash; a run context scopes the run, it does not carry the prompt. Use <strong>Agent Input Mapping</strong> for that.</p>',
'',
'<p>Unlike Agent Input Mapping, this is re-sent on <em>every</em> turn, not just the first. A later turn may add a key but may not change one &mdash; see <strong>Run Context Drift</strong>.</p>',
'',
'<p>Leave blank to run unbound.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479219876797279721)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(865188135557955928)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>20
,p_display_sequence=>200
,p_static_id=>'run_context_drift'
,p_prompt=>'Run Context Drift'
,p_attribute_type=>'SELECT LIST'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_default_value=>'error'
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_depending_on_attribute_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479219325836276697)
,p_depending_on_has_to_exist=>true
,p_depending_on_condition_type=>'NOT_NULL'
,p_lov_type=>'STATIC'
,p_attribute_group_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(479227950721456087)
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>What to do when <strong>Agent Run Context</strong> resolves to different values than the ones this conversation is already bound to &mdash; typically because the user navigated to another record while the chat was open.</p>',
'',
'<p>UC AI binds the context on a conversation&rsquo;s first turn. A later turn may add a key, but changing one is refused: the persisted messages, and any memory files, were written under the original binding, so silently re-targeting them would expos'
||'e one record&rsquo;s conversation to another.</p>',
'',
'<ul>',
'  <li><strong>Refuse the turn and explain why</strong> (default) &mdash; nothing is sent, and a notice above the composer tells the user the conversation is tied to different data. Safe: nothing is lost without the user choosing it.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Start a new conversation</strong> &mdash; the region silently opens a fresh conversation bound to the new values and sends the message there. Right for &ldquo;talk to this record&rdquo; pages; the visible history of the old conversation'
||' is gone, and there is no history UI to get it back.</li>',
'  <li><strong>Keep the original binding</strong> &mdash; the change is ignored and the conversation keeps answering under what its first turn bound. Matches how Agent Input Mapping stops applying after the first message.</li>',
'</ul>',
'',
'<p>Only relevant when Agent Run Context is set. Adding a <em>new</em> key is never a conflict and is always allowed.</p>'))
);
